<!--
  Paste this block into the host repo's CLAUDE.md. It is the RULE half of
  the .cld toolkit -- the half nothing mechanical can enforce. The
  checkers catch a stale index; only the rule makes an agent CHECK an
  index before hunting, and update one in the same commit.

  Adjust the paths if you vendored the toolkit somewhere other than the
  repo root.
-->

## Directory Indexes

Each directory has an `index.cld` describing its contents.
Format and rules: `spec/dir-index-format.txt`.

- When looking for a file, check `index.cld` in the relevant directory
  first -- or run the `index-find` skill, which greps every index at
  once.
- When working in a directory that has no `index.cld`, create one
  before finishing.
- Keep `index.cld` current: update it in the same commit when you add,
  remove, rename, or edit a file in that directory.

## Symbol Indexes

Each source file has a `<filename>.cld` symbol index in the same
directory. Format and rules: `spec/file-index-format.txt`.

- When looking for a method, class, or API, check `<filename>.cld`
  before grepping source -- or run the `filename-find` skill.
- Before naming a new symbol, run `filename-dupecheck` on the name.
- Keep `<filename>.cld` current: update it in the same commit when you
  add, remove, rename, or change the signature or behaviour of any
  symbol.

## The Gate

`scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit` runs both index checkers over the staged
diff and blocks a commit whose indexes have gone stale. Install it once
per clone with `./scripts/git-hooks/install.sh`. Run
`index-audit-partial` before committing to see a block coming.

There is no sanctioned bypass. The rule is fix the index.
